/*!
    \page index.html
    \title QtCraft API

    QtCraft is a voxel sandbox game built with Qt 6 (C++23, Qt Quick, QRhi). Client and server
    are separate programs even in single player: the game runs its server in the same process
    (QcLocalServerHost) and talks to it only through protocol messages, as it talks to a server
    over the network.

    This reference is generated by QDoc from the comments in the headers and QML files. How the
    game is played is in the \l {QtCraft Handbook}{handbook}.

    \section1 Libraries

    Each library may use only the libraries listed before it (with the exceptions named on its
    page); the client libraries never see a server type.

    \table
    \header \li Library \li Content
    \row \li \l {qc_common} \li Shared by client and server: coordinates, chunks, the content
         registry, physics, the protocol, the handbook.
    \row \li \l {qc_network} \li TCP and TLS transport of the protocol frames.
    \row \li \l {qc_worldgen} \li World generation: generators, terrain, structures, villages,
         the showcase world.
    \row \li \l {qc_server} \li The authoritative server: tick, world, chunks, mobs, plants,
         commands, saving.
    \row \li \l {qc_worlds} \li Running worlds for the game and the headless server: the local
         server, the world library, mods.
    \row \li \l {qc_clientcore} \li The client without GUI: session, prediction, meshing, light,
         camera, textures, sound synthesis.
    \row \li \l {qc_audio} \li Sound output of the graphical client.
    \row \li \l {qc_app_core} \li The Qt Quick client: controllers for QML, rendering, input.
    \row \li \l {qtcraft_headless} \li The headless server, bots and the control interface.
    \row \li \l {QtCraft QML Types} \li The QML module \c QtCraft: screens, HUD and controls.
    \endtable

    \l {All C++ classes}
*/

/*!
    \page classes.html
    \title All C++ classes

    \generatelist classes
*/

